        "source_sha256": "6231909ac3a619bcc6a76eeb7ec258431b3f415c87af650286ca983478db16eb",
        "text": "top of page\nLog In\nDonate Now\nA Parent's Voice.\nAn Advocate's Heart.\nA Leader for Every Student.\nDONATE NOW\n# Alida Fisher\nSFUSD parent of more than 20+ years\nSpecial education advocate\nFormer foster parent\nDaughter and granddaughter of teachers\nCurrent School Board Member\nBefore joining the Board, Alida spent years advocating for students and families through district committees and working groups. She built coalitions with educators, district leaders, and elected officials to strengthen our schools and improve student outcomes.\nAlida is running for reelection to the San Fransico School Board to continue building strong, equitable, and student-centered public schools for every child in San Francisco.\nRead Alida's Story\n## Alida's Core Values\nAlida is focused on the issues that matter most to our students, families, educators, and our future.\n### Strong Public Schools\nin Every Community\nAcademic excellence rooted in equity remains at the center of Alida's work. Alida is working towards a future where every SFUSD student has access to high-quality instruction, meaningful supports, and individualized pathways that allow them to thrive.\nFor more than a decade, both as a commissioner and previously as a parent advocate, Alida has worked alongside families, educators, and administrators to push for high-quality, evidence-based curriculum aligned with the science of reading. That advocacy led to the adoption of our new literacy curriculum, and we are now in our third full year of implementation.\n​\nLearn more about Alida's work to improve student outcomes here.\n### Community Voice at the\nHeart of all Decisions\nCommunity engagement is what led Alida to her role on the Board. As a parent advocate, she places a huge emphasis on collaboration.\nAlida is a former advisory committee chair and a founding member of the Joint Advisory Alignment Committee, which brings leadership teams from the parent committees and District leaders together to elevate and amplify our common goals: inclusion and support for all students.\n### Schools where All Students feel Safe, Welcome, and Included\nAlida is focused on the issues that matter most to our families and our future: investing in our schools and educators to ensure every child has the opportunity to succeed.\n​\nAlida is a proud leader in SFUSD's commitment to affirming and celebrating the diversity within our community. From the celebration the 10th anniversary of AAALI, the African American Achievement and Leadership Initiative, to the resolutions to authorizing the Queer and Trans Parent Advisory Council (QTPAC) and the Fa'aSāmoa Initiative, she is committed to providing the supports and protections to students and their families; and more.\n​\nDiversity is one of San Francisco’s greatest assets. It makes our schools, our classrooms, and our communities more thoughtful, innovative, and resilient. By working together throughout our schools to invest in all students, especially those who have historically been underserved, we create stronger outcomes not only for individual children, but for the entire city.\nProviding a high-quality education to every student is at the heart of why the SFUSD Board of Education adopted the Student Outcomes Focused Governance (SOFG) model and committed to prioritizing our three core goals: improving third grade reading proficiency, strengthening eighth grade math proficiency, and ensuring students graduate prepared for college and careers.\n​\n​\nIn Alida's first term as commissioner, the Board has:\nAdopted a balanced 2025–26 budget while advancing a multi-year fiscal stabilization plan, moving SFUSD from negative to qualified certification and positioning the district for positive certification next school year;\nAdopted new curriculum in English language arts, math, social studies, history, and ethnic studies, providing educators with stronger instructional tools and creating greater stability and coherence across the district;\nModernized outdated financial and HR systems through the implementation of Frontline and Red Rover, improving operational effectiveness and helping ensure employees are paid accurately and on time;\nPassed a $790 million bond to modernize schools and build a new central food preparation kitchen;\nReached multi-year agreements with all labor partners, including historic dependent health care benefits for educators; and\nSuccessfully implemented a major districtwide Transitional Kindergarten expansion, increasing access to early learning opportunities for families across San Francisco.\n​\n​\n​\n### Good Governance as the Foundation of the Work\n## Join the Movement\nWinning a second term will take people power: neighbors, families, educators, and community members coming together to build the future we want for SFUSD.\nEvery volunteer makes a difference, whether you can knock doors, make calls, spread the word, or bring others into the campaign.\nFill out the form below, and someone from our team will be in touch soon. Together, we can win on November 3rd!\nVolunteer Today\nbottom of page",
